        "2026-11-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/process/ask-the-person.bpmn#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "process Process_AskThePerson",
      "prov:value": "The discussion itself (say what is decided and why, lay out the options with their costs, recommend one, ask ONE question, follow up narrower, apply a default only if allowed, record what is still open) is bootstrap's `Process_HumanAgentDiscussion`, which cat-harness reaches through `needs: [\"bootstrap\"]`. Before this, the same steps were drawn here a second time. What this process adds is the harness's own part: the composed question with lettered options and glossed names, the sibling hand-back, and the delivery rule that the full question goes in the chat FIRST and the card second."
    },
    {
      "@id": "processes/process/ask-the-person.bpmn#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "exclusiveGateway GW_Discussing",
      "prov:value": "A sibling that is not sure takes `no`: one extra copy costs a line, a missed card stalls a decision (owner, 2026-10-31: \"sublings not raising cards to main\", cat-harness#861).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
